From fd503a492d381687c143b7085ea79ebce58dcdc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iceland-dev <dev@iceland.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:16:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tools: virt: gunyah: add VM smoke test and record
 verification results

gh_vmtest.py drives /dev/gunyah directly (python3, no dependencies): it
builds a minimal guest DTB, lends 4 MiB of anonymous memory, sets the
boot PC, adds one vCPU, starts the VM and runs it until the 16-byte
guest payload exits via PSCI SYSTEM_OFF, optionally after an MMIO store
to an unmapped GPA or a store into a second, host-shared binding.
gh_trace.sh wraps a run in kprobe events on the demand-paging path.

Documentation/virt/gunyah/port_adaptations.md gains the results on the
OnePlus Pad 4, the guest-DTB rules the resource manager enforces without
saying so (RAM node must be exactly /memory, timer PPI CPU mask must
match the vCPU count) and the firmware limitations found: unprotected
image parcels are refused with MAP_FAILED, a protected VM cannot use
host-shared bindings as guest RAM (hypervisor DENIED on addrspace_map),
and the RM log is unimplemented.
---
 Documentation/virt/gunyah/port_adaptations.md |  78 +++++++-
 tools/virt/gunyah/gh_trace.sh                 |  28 +++
 tools/virt/gunyah/gh_vmtest.py                | 187 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 288 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 tools/virt/gunyah/gh_trace.sh
 create mode 100755 tools/virt/gunyah/gh_vmtest.py

